{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":31830,"duration_api_ms":31830,"is_error":false,"result":"Investigating how scores map to letter grades in the codebase.\nBoundary bug: `letter_grade` used `> 90` instead of `>= 90`, so 90 mapped to B. Fixing it.\nThe issue was in `letter_grade` in `repo/grading.py`. The A cutoff used **strictly greater than** 90 (`score > 90`), so a score of **exactly 90** fell through to the B band (`score >= 80`).\n\n**Change:** use `score >= 90` for an A.\n\nReports that use `letter_grade` (including `grade_summary` in `repo/rows.py`, which takes the max score) will now show **A** for 90. Tests pass.","session_id":"9525d707-b0a1-470d-829c-013fb4992a06","request_id":"3be656fd-f894-4bae-afe7-53a1f07c396b","usage":{"inputTokens":11170,"outputTokens":685,"cacheReadTokens":46624,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
